WEBVTT

00:01:58.461 --> 00:02:00.754
in the same way you want
people to respond to it.

00:02:00.778 --> 00:02:03.135
They're going to be looking
and listening for cues

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:04.877
on what the appropriate response is.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:07.219
Is this something
that you want to be celebrated?

00:02:07.243 --> 00:02:08.486
I'm trans!

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.369
Or do you want to just address it
and move on with your life?

00:02:11.393 --> 00:02:12.826
Oh, by the way, I'm trans.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.526
There's no one right way
to say it for everybody.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:18.126
What's most important here
is what's right for you.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.313
Another note,

00:02:19.337 --> 00:02:21.446
we're not going to be able
to control the way

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:23.193
in which everybody responds to this.

00:02:23.217 --> 00:02:24.781
But what we do have control over

00:02:24.805 --> 00:02:26.833
is how they understand
our own relationship

00:02:26.857 --> 00:02:28.294
with this part of who we are.

00:02:28.318 --> 00:02:30.190
So now that we know what we want to say